2026-01-15 00:02:41 | INFO | Q165 id=BV1ps4y1w7Wr_00-00-00_00-00-10 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=To estimate the depth of the well, we need to consider the time it takes for the sound to travel from the stone hitting the bottom of the well back to the surface. The sound travels at approximately 343 meters per second in air.\n\n1. The sound travels down to the bottom of the well and back up to the surface.\n2. The time taken for the sound to travel down and back up is given as 200-300 milliseconds (ms).\n\nLet's calculate the depth:\n\n- Time for one-way trip (down or up) = 200-300 ms / 2 = 100-150 ms\n- Distance for one-way trip = Speed × Time\n- Speed = 343 m/s\n- Time = 100-150 ms = 0.1-0.15 seconds\n\nNow, calculate the distance for one-way trip:\n- Distance = 343 m/s × 0.1 s = 34.3 m\n- Distance = 343 m/s × 0.15 s = 51.45 m\n\nThe depth of the well is the distance for one-way trip, which is between 34.3 m and 51.45 m.\n\nGiven the choices:\nA) 0-100m\nB) 100-200m\nC) 200-300m\nD) 300-400m\n\nThe depth of the well falls within the range of 34.3 m to 51.45 m, which corresponds to option C.\n\nAnswer: \boxed{C}
